WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.744
Total views double each day. The running totals are fifteen, thirty one, sixty three, one hundred and twenty seven. When does the total first pass one hundred? On day seven.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:25.809
In a geometric series, n sits in a power, like r to the n. To bring n down, take logarithms, or logs. The rule: log of r to the n is n times log r.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:36.776
When r is a fraction, its log is negative. Dividing an inequality by a negative number reverses the sign. This step loses many marks.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:46.322
These questions ask for the least n so that a sum or a term passes a target. You use logs, then round to a whole number.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:57.736
Step one: write the sum or term using a and r, and make the inequality. Step two: get the power of r on its own, before taking logs.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:07.205
Step three: take logs, bring n down, and divide by log r. If r is a fraction, log r is negative, so reverse the sign.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:14.095
Step four: round to a whole number the right way, and check. The trap is not reversing the sign.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:32.088
June twenty twenty four, paper one. The first term is three hundred and twenty and the common ratio is one quarter. Using logarithms, find the least n such that S n is greater than four hundred and twenty six point six. Four marks.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:43.068
Step one: S n is a times one minus r to the n, over one minus r. That is twelve hundred and eighty over three, times one minus one quarter to the n.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:51.968
Step two: divide by twelve hundred and eighty over three. Then one quarter to the n is less than one over six thousand four hundred.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:59.537
Step three: take logs. N times log of one quarter is less than log of one over six thousand four hundred.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:11.943
Step four: log of one quarter is negative, so dividing reverses the sign. N is greater than log six thousand four hundred over log four. That is six point three two.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:25.732
Reject a tempting route. Not reversing the sign gives n less than six point three two, so n is six. But S six is four hundred and twenty six point five six, not above the target.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:32.221
So the least whole number is seven. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:44.893
Another mistake is taking logs too early. Log of one minus a power is not log one minus log of the power. Isolate the power first.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:03:07.794
Now you try, from November twenty twenty three. The first term is sixteen. From part a, r is plus or minus thirteen over twenty five, and r is positive. The sum to n terms is greater than thirty three. Using logarithms, find the least n. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:22.474
R is thirteen over twenty five. S n is one hundred over three, times one minus r to the n. Greater than thirty three gives r to the n less than nought point nought one.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:33.936
Take logs. The log of thirteen over twenty five is negative, so reverse the sign. N is greater than seven point oh four. The least whole number is eight.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:45.920
The common wrong answer is seven, from rounding seven point oh four down. But S seven is thirty two point nine nine, not above thirty three. Least means round up.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.887
Remember the method. Isolate the power, take logs, reverse the sign, and round.
